@@ -22,6 +22,8 @@ All notable changes to Packeteer are documented here. Versions are Git tags on `
 
 ### Added
 
+- Probe scheduler and passive prefix counts (#125). Due prefixes are probed in priority order (urgent, then a shorter interval, then the engine interval, then a longer tail). Each prefix is stored when its probes finish, so a round that hits its deadline keeps those results and leaves an unfinished prefix on its previous result. Staleness stays per result. The flow window's exact 20,000 cells are unchanged (probe targets, commit volume, anomaly counters). Each bucket adds a fixed HyperLogLog (4096 registers, 4 KiB; about 120 KiB for a 5-minute window) of every prefix offered to it, including ones the exact map refused. `packeteer_probe_prefix_commits` and `packeteer_flow_prefixes_tracked` are on `/metrics`. The `pr` and weekly `soak` load profiles require at least 180,000 active prefixes per hour and 50,000 passively tracked prefixes. `rss_growth_mb` stays 384. An opt-in `rate` profile (20,000 prefixes, 100 packets per second, 375 pinned targets) reports the same figures and is not what CI runs. Every packet still waits on `probe.rate_limit_pps`. Nothing is announced. Observe stays the default. The learned-RIB check, allowlist, cap, community and NO_EXPORT, hold time, and withdraw rules are unchanged. Rollback: revert this change.
+
 - Outage detection from traceroute hop ASNs and alternate provider paths (#124). The `outage` source maps each stable hop from a per-provider indirect trace to the origin ASN of the longest matching learned prefix (the last ASN; a default route is not a match; no external data). Add-path and BMP paths that are not the selected route's own path are correlated beside the native AS path. An ASN that appears only in hop data opens an `outage.as` incident. An ASN that appears only on a non-native provider's path, when that provider is the degraded one, is attributed to that provider instead of a circuit. Thresholds, events, and `max_targets` are unchanged. With no traces and no alternate paths the correlation is the native AS path alone. Nothing is announced. Observe stays the default. Every new packet still waits on `probe.rate_limit_pps`. Rollback: revert this change. Removing the `outage` source, or `probe.indirect`, leaves announcements untouched.
 
 - FRR lab checks per-cause `local_pref` on the edge (#132 follow-up). `lab/packeteer.yaml` sets `local_pref_cause.performance: 260`. `lab/e2e.sh` requires LocPrf 260 while the route is present and requires it gone after SIGTERM and SIGKILL. `lab/checkroute` still defaults to 250 for the commit and cost labs.
